<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.record.wins ~ a person settles one standoff toward the records

A standoff names a carrier whose file and records disagree while no rule picks. `take-records <uri> --key <key>` writes the records' render over that file; `keep-records` does the same where drafts stand, and lets the drafts go. The key comes from the alert (`lares shore` prints it), and an answer that names a state that moved takes nothing: the island refuses by name.

SETTLING STAYS A HAND ACT: the verb reads the hand behind this command before it asks or runs anything; an AI harness on its branch refuses `hand-act-only`, an unreadable branch `hand-unattested`, each naming the command the operator runs, and `yes=true` approves nothing by itself. A terminal asks `Proceed? [y/N]` (the file's present bytes give way to the records' render); a JSON call off a terminal needs `yes=true`. `face=N` answers a lit sibling's standoff without wearing it; `--bag` narrows the carrier's bag.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ take-the-records · a-siblings-standoff

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`take-the-records` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example key/<key> ~ the records' render overwrites the file`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-siblings-standoff` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example key/<key> face/2 ~ answer a lit sibling's standoff without wearing it`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri · key · bag · face · yes

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/lar-address needs/required seat/1 as/<uri> ~ the carrier at the standoff`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`key` params=`takes/key needs/required ~ the standoff's key, as lares shore printed it`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`bag` params=`takes/bag-uri ~ the bag that holds the carrier`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`face` params=`takes/handle-index ~ a lit sibling's shore, by handle index`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`yes` params=`kind/switch ~ name the intent for a call off a terminal; approves nothing by itself`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

